# The wiki is published to another repository and read by Wiki.js. Keep it LF
# everywhere: a page that comes back from a checkout with CRLF silently breaks
# the screenshot markers and the front matter parsing, which is a bug you find
# by wondering why an image never appeared.
# Text only. `wiki/** text eol=lf` was wrong and briefly stored every
# screenshot as line-ending-converted text: a PNG header begins PNG
,
# so the conversion ate the  and the committed image was three bytes short
# and unreadable. Working files were untouched, but a fresh checkout would
# have handed someone four broken images.
wiki/**/*.md   text eol=lf
wiki/**/*.css  text eol=lf

# Everything else under wiki/ is an asset. Never touch the bytes.
wiki/**/*.png  -text
wiki/**/*.jpg  -text
wiki/**/*.jpeg -text
wiki/**/*.gif  -text
wiki/**/*.webp -text
wiki/**/*.svg  -text
